    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14419" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dissŏcĭābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		dissocio. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>separating</i>, <i>dividing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oceanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 3, 22</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>that cannot be
			united</i>, <i>irreconcilable</i>, <i>incompatible</i>: olim res miscere,
			<i><span class="en">Tac. Agr.
			3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. in Ruf. 2, 238</span></i>
			.</div>
